Privacy Policy
Last Updated: 27th Feb 2026

Daily Grace (“we,” “our,” or “us”) operates the Daily Grace mobile application (the “App”). This Privacy Policy explains how we handle information when you use the App.

About Daily Grace
Daily Grace provides one scripture-backed affirmation each day, including a declaration to speak, the supporting Bible verse, a guided prayer, a reflection prompt, and a private journal feature. The App contains 365 affirmations across 10 categories: Identity in Christ, Strength & Courage, Peace & Rest, Healing & Restoration, Purpose & Calling, Gratitude & Joy, Faith & Trust, Love & Worth, Provision & Abundance, and Victory & Overcoming.

Information We Collect
We do not require account creation. We do not collect personal information such as your name, email address, contact details, or precise location.

We may automatically collect limited non-personal information, including:

Device type

Operating system

Anonymous usage data

Crash diagnostics

If you enable push notifications, a device token may be stored solely for the purpose of sending daily affirmation reminders.

Journal and “Release to God” Feature
Journal entries and text written in the “Release to God” feature are stored locally on your device. We do not access, read, store, or transmit your personal reflections to our servers.

In-App Purchase
Daily Grace offers a one-time purchase to unlock full access. Payments are processed securely through Apple’s App Store. We do not collect, store, or have access to your payment information.

Third-Party Services
The App may use Apple-provided services such as analytics or crash reporting. These services may collect information in accordance with their own privacy policies.

Data Security
We take reasonable measures to protect any limited technical data associated with the App.

Children’s Privacy
Daily Grace does not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13.

Changes to This Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any updates will be reflected by revising the “Last Updated” date.

